# Ignition browser E2E

Scaffolded by `ign e2e init` against `__IGN_GATEWAY_URL__`.

Playwright drives a real browser against the gateway. The login form is
never touched: `global-setup.mjs` asks the CLI for a session and hands
Playwright the resulting `storageState`.

## Run it

```sh
npm test              # headless
npm run test:headed   # watch the browser
npm run test:ui       # Playwright's UI mode
npm run report        # open the last HTML report
```

Diagnose the setup at any time:

```sh
ign e2e doctor --project __IGN_PROJECT__
```

## What global setup does

1. **`ign session login --json`** — runs the gateway's native OIDC
   login and writes `data.storage_state` to `.auth/state.json`.
   `playwright.config.mjs` points `use.storageState` at that file, so
   every browser context starts already authenticated.
2. **`ign testing run --project __IGN_PROJECT__ --json`** — runs the
   gateway's own Jython suite FIRST and throws if the verdict is not
   `passed`, aborting before a single page is opened. A browser failure
   caused by broken gateway-side code is an expensive way to learn
   something one HTTP call already knew. Set
   `IGN_E2E_SKIP_GATEWAY_TESTS=1` to skip this gate.

Both steps surface the CLI's own stderr and name its exit code: **3** a
missing password, **5** rejected credentials, **6** a red suite.

## Environment

| Variable | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `IGNITION_URL` | Gateway base URL. Overrides the baked-in `__IGN_GATEWAY_URL__`. |
| `IGNITION_PASSWORD` | **Required.** The gateway password, read by `ign session login`. Never a flag, never in a file here. |
| `IGNITION_USER` | Gateway username. Defaults to `admin`. |
| `IGNITION_TOKEN` | API token for the `lib/gateway.mjs` helpers (`X-Ignition-API-Token`). |
| `IGN_BIN` | Path to the `ign` binary. Defaults to `ign` on `PATH`. |
| `IGN_E2E_SKIP_GATEWAY_TESTS` | Set to `1` to skip the gateway-suite gate in global setup. |
| `IGNITION_ALLOW_INSECURE_LOCAL` | Set to `true` to apply the loopback TLS relaxation to a non-loopback host. See below. |

## TLS

`lib/gateway.mjs` disables certificate verification **only** when the
gateway host is `localhost`, `127.0.0.1`, or `::1` — and prints one
warning to stderr when it does. A self-signed certificate on your own
machine is a papercut; the same relaxation pointed at a remote gateway
silently removes the guarantee HTTPS exists to provide.

For a remote gateway behind a private CA, do **not** set
`IGNITION_ALLOW_INSECURE_LOCAL`. Point Node at the CA instead:

```sh
export NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS=/path/to/company-ca.pem
```

## Files

| File | What it is |
|---|---|
| `playwright.config.mjs` | Runner config: `baseURL`, the 180 s timeout, `globalSetup`, `use.storageState`. |
| `global-setup.mjs` | The two-step bootstrap described above. |
| `lib/gateway.mjs` | `readTags`, `writeTags`, `runScript`, `waitForTag` over the gateway's testing routes. |
| `tests/example.spec.mjs` | A tag round trip and a Perspective shell check. |
| `.auth/state.json` | **Generated, gitignored.** Holds a live session cookie. |

Edit `tests/example.spec.mjs` or add your own `tests/*.spec.mjs`.
